From dd5a767b3581dbef61ff6c3937b8824de26ff9e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:19:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(tui_gateway): one user row per hold-queued
 prompt.submit

A prompt.submit queued behind the core-update admission hold (queued_reason=core_update) wrote its user
row at accept (marked _queued_prompt), then the drain's _replace_queued_user_row_for_turn appended an
identical row at the end and deactivated the accept row. One submit, one turn, two user rows in
state.db (live on hermes-hub 2026-11-12: msgs 1217133 + 1217162, t_01a1c8d8a5c1f725).

Re-placement exists to keep alternation when the in-flight turn's rows landed AFTER the accept row
(busy-queue [uA, uB, aA]). When nothing landed after it, the dispatching envelope now adopts the
accept row in place: one guarded UPDATE drops the never-drained marker only while it is still the
session's last active row (follows a compaction re-sequenced clone via resolve_active_row_id), and
the turn adopts that row through the existing _submit_user_row slot, so the flush writes nothing.
Any later active row, a still-queued (non-dispatching) envelope, or a store error falls back to the
existing re-append path unchanged. Durable-at-accept and restart retirement (#125577) are unchanged.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_update_hold_submit_queue.py
test_hold_queued_submit_then_replay_writes_exactly_one_user_row (and the compaction clone case) FAIL
on the old drain (2 rows: accept inactive+marked, re-append active) and pass now; controls: later row
still re-placed, still-queued envelope keeps its marker. Isolated serve repro (own HERMES_HOME, fake
LLM): before 2 rows (1 inactive) / 1 turn, after 1 row / 1 turn; non-queued submit 1 row.
Mutants: 14 killed, 0 survived. Related suites (queue, persistence, restart retire, admission,
retry, server, hermes_state/) green.
